<p>What follows is reproduced in John's own words, exactly as he wrote them: nothing edited, softened, or left out. Unlike his first three books, this one gives no chapter divisions; after a preface and a page of epigraphs it runs as one continuous sequence of roughly forty-five titled stories threaded through with untitled barroom vignettes, each headed only with the book's own title, "Third Stool from the Rear," as if overheard from a stool at the end of the bar. The book numbers its own pages 1 through 52 and gives no table of contents. For readability on the web it is split here into five parts of roughly equal length, breaking at whichever vignette falls closest to an even division of the book's pages; the part numbers and titles are ours, not John's. Numbers in parentheses are the book's own printed page numbers.</p>

<p>The book's dedication, "Because I Love You, That's Why!," addressed to John's wife Inez Schriver Jackson, along with a photograph of her and one of John himself at the Palo Alto tunnel in 1949, is printed on the book's final leaf rather than at the front; it is kept in that position here, at the end of Part V.</p>

<h2>Contents</h2>

<p>The book gives no table of contents of its own. The five parts below are this site's own division, with the stories and vignettes each part contains.</p>

<p><strong><a href="/writings/third-stool-from-the-rear/part-i/">Part I</a></strong> (pp. 1&ndash;10): The Perils of Adolescence; Brotherly Love; "Sure He's Okay, I Saw Him a Couple of Months Ago"; The Last Straw on the Camel's Back; To Honor &amp; to Cherish; Didn't Have to, the Boot Had a Hole in It; A Rude Awakening; with barroom vignettes throughout.</p>

<p><strong><a href="/writings/third-stool-from-the-rear/part-ii/">Part II</a></strong> (pp. 11&ndash;20): Lynn Rides a Hellcat and She Ghost Bareback; Board Stiff; Chalk One Up for Blackberry; Smiles Forgot to Smile; Fiddling Around with the Judge; Lou Oppey's Snow Bred Red McClures; Long Distance Indigestion; with barroom vignettes throughout.</p>

<p><strong><a href="/writings/third-stool-from-the-rear/part-iii/">Part III</a></strong> (pp. 21&ndash;30): Low Pressure Waterworks; Bernie Folds His Sails; Mine Is Not to Question Why; Bill Graduates to Higher Mathematics; with barroom vignettes throughout.</p>

<p><strong><a href="/writings/third-stool-from-the-rear/part-iv/">Part IV</a></strong> (pp. 31&ndash;41): Better Knock the Next Time You Drop In; Fire in the Hole and Marmot Burgers; We Remember Christie; I Just Put a Little Salt on His Tail; with barroom vignettes throughout.</p>

<p><strong><a href="/writings/third-stool-from-the-rear/part-v/">Part V</a></strong> (pp. 42&ndash;52): Marriage is a Partnership; Two Tramps and a Dog from Silverton; Just One More Round, Dear Lord; a tommyknocker poem and two further closing poems; a roll of the top team miners of John's era; the Synopsis; and the dedication.</p>

